  "id": "discrete-variable",
  "term": "discrete variable",
  "definition": "A discrete variable is a variable that can take only a limited set of distinct values rather than any value along a continuum. All qualitative variables are discrete, and some quantitative variables are also discrete, although variables with many possible separate values may sometimes be treated as continuous in practice.",
